{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "euclid-ghosts — a euclidean backbone with a Markov chain filling the gaps.",
    "",
    "Two generators drive the same four tracks, doing opposite jobs:",
    "",
    "  grid    euclidpercs — the skeleton. Syncopated 3-pulse kick, backbeat snare,",
    "          quarter-note hats. Identical every pass; this is the thing you can",
    "          count against.",
    "  ghosts  markovpercs — the decoration. Quiet (velocity 0.32) and sparse, and",
    "          every hit lands off the beat, so it fills gaps instead of competing.",
    "          Patched to snare/hats/percs only — never the kick.",
    "",
    "Because each track loads only its own category, a ghost hit for a category a",
    "track doesn't own is simply silent. No filtering, just routing.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /grid                      the fixed skeleton",
    "  /ghosts                    the decoration (..s...sh.sh..ps.)",
    "  /ghosts velocity=0.6 4b    push the ghosts forward until they compete",
    "  /ghosts velocity=0.32 4b   and back",
    "  /ghosts seed=random        re-roll only the decoration; the grid holds",
    "  /grid dropout=0.4 8b       thin the skeleton and let the ghosts show through",
    "  /grid preset=fourfloor at=cycle    swap the backbone on the next bar",
    "",
    "Mute either one to hear what it was doing: /snare stop at=cycle, or unpatch."
  ],
  "clock": {"bpm": 92, "loopLengthBeats": 4},
